@Eloston I understand. I went for the radical approach because I am not very well aware of how useful/necessary these APIs are. For the client rects I am going for a randomisation approach, as mentioned in this [nice paper](http://www.gsd.inesc-id.pt/~mpc/pubs/fingerprinting-trustcom2016.pdf).

For the others I might stay on the "axe" approach, at least until I am aware of the consequences.

As per flags, sorry that does not match with the effort I want to put in the development of these mitigations, but I agree that it would be better.
